iv. 	Before I return to silence, I’d like to share the directive of the group associated 
with this writing, more as something which has developed alongside it rather than 
something the writing was built for: As this group has popularized, it’s clear our small, 
quickly made about section is not close to enough. The group was founded after the 
realization of creative corruption in late mid-August of this year, buying and selling 
myths, and a want to approach the community from a new perspective. This group is not 
a community, it is part of the community; we are not forming a large hierarchy, doing 
elaborate ranks, nor are we prioritizing events or hunts. This group is here to inspire 
conversation, development of community concepts, finding what the art is in a myth, 
what the community is for. For this reason, SEMATOC has written an extended essay 
analyzing the community (NOT intended to be explicitly associated with the MECE), and 
conversation or more writing is expected to follow. 
  	There will be no extremely functional Discord for the group; although it would be 
good for conversation, we wish for people to engage in the concepts provided by us away 
from us, perhaps spreading the idea of this building of concepts to other shards of the 
community. So, this community will be having a few events for fun, some hunts, but 
these things are not the purpose, even if you want everybody to see the writing. The 
group is directed at myths, mostly comprising the ranks, and the ambassadors will be 
the leaders of the group, rather than one or a few people with extreme power. The 
myths will push the ideology of the group or expand the perspectives of the community 
with their influence. To elaborate on rankings, we’ll do categorical rankings, and above 
those, ranks directly associated with the group itself and its functions. We believe that 
myths can be much more than what they are, or ever have been, for the sake of the 
community we have enjoyed for so long.

